\begin{theorem}[Supported straightening in the lower handle indices]
\label{thm:lower-handle-straightening}
\uses{thm:protected-wall-core,def:generalized-dehn,thm:protected-prime-replacement,def:marked-relative-torus-rigidity}
\lean{PoincareMT.M76.lowerCases_of_wall_dehn_prime}
The Wall, generalized Dehn, protected replacement, and relative rigidity
constructions give Hamilton chart-handle straightening for every coordinate
subset $J\subset\{0,1,2\}$ with $|J|\leq2$. The correction makes the
original chart finite PL on the unit ball; its isotopy fixes the cylinder
frontier, its complement, and the radius-two exterior pointwise.
\end{theorem}

